| `tests/integration/test_install_sources_gate.py` | Fails an install that ignores config/project.json `install_sources`: it runs `make fe-install` and `make fe-browsers` on a copy with stub `node` and `npm`, and every workflow step with a pip, pip3, `python -m pip`, npm install or ci alias, or playwright install command under `bash -e` with stub tools, and requires the configured URL as `--index-url`, `--registry` or `PLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST` when set and none of them when null; a pnpm or yarn install, an installer named by path or under sudo, and a step that fails under the stubs are faults; a URL user part must stop the target before npm runs and never be shown. | `make test` | [`install_sources.python_index`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`install_sources.npm_registry`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`install_sources.browser_download_host`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Runs stubs, not the real tools, so it proves the flag is passed and not that a mirror serves it. Not the URL bound itself: `tests/unit/scripts/test_install_sources.py` judges the values the loader refuses. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
